  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 315 AM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nFriday...There may be some lingering flooding problems in the \nmorning, but convective coverage should be diurnally waning into the \nmidday. Boundary placement should make for high temp variance from \nthe upper 70s north, to the upper 80s in the far south. Timing the \nnext ridge-riding short wave may bring yet another MCS in from the \nwest by late afternoon and into Friday evening. This would bring \nmore damaging wind threats as well as more heavy rain to a \npotentially water sensitive CWA and there may be a need of another \nflood watch. Area creeks and rivers could be really on the rise at \nthat time as well, will have to keep the hydrological aspects more \nin mind as well as the severe risks.\n\nSaturday through Wednesday...Latest ensemble and upper jet trends \nsuggest the upper ridge and heat dome to get pressed eastward \ntemporarily maintaining the ring of fire for the weekend with the local \narea dangerously near the periphery through at least Sunday. Storm \nchances will continue as well as a hot humid Saturday in store, but \nthen some signs early next week of upper ridge retro-grade allowing \nfor more of a northwest flow push down the upper MS RVR Valley. A \nresultant drier and cooler Monday would be much welcome by then.",
